-- rasa_route_delete_trimmed_landmark_items.sql
--
-- WHY (owner SQL - the anon key cannot delete rows):
--
-- The demo landmarks were trimmed to at most 2 dishes each. The excess 394
-- items were first only soft-hidden (landmark_item.is_removed = true) - but
-- the app's LANDMARK DETAIL query (SubmittedLandmarkRepository.
-- getSubmittedLandmarkById) does NOT filter is_removed, so those dishes still
-- appeared on the landmark pages (many duplicate Cendol pictures). Only the
-- report picker filters the flag today.
--
-- This deletes EXACTLY the soft-hidden demo rows listed below, so the
-- duplicates disappear from EVERY screen. The 606 visible items
-- (each with a unique photo) are not touched.
-- Run tools/seed_landmarks.py --prune-orphans afterwards to remove their
-- now-unreferenced photos from storage.
--
-- NOTE: not reversible for these rows (plain demo data - the seed tool can
-- regenerate landmarks when needed).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. PREVIEW
